course: dictionary
lesson: 15675
title: A tickler tickles, puzzles or makes you laugh
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To tickle means to touch someone lightly so they giggle. A tickler is a person or thing that tickles. But this word often has a second, playful meaning, so look at the words around it to find out which one is meant.
explain: «Sam sat with his puzzle book, stuck on a brain tickler.» The clue is puzzle book: a brain tickler is a fun puzzle that makes you think hard. «Grandpa told a rib tickler that made the whole table laugh.» The clue is laugh: a rib tickler is a very funny joke.
explain: Words like these are informal, which means they are used in chatty talk and fun books. Always check your meaning in the sentence. If a puzzle fits, a tickle would not make sense there.
fact: Tickler comes from the word tickle.
fact: A brain tickler is a fun puzzle or riddle that makes you think.
fact: A rib tickler is a very funny joke.
fact: A tickler can also be a small problem that bothers you, like a tickle in your throat.
fact: A tickler file is an old American reminder system of notes about things to do on certain days.
exercise: «Ella solved the brain tickler in ten minutes.» What is a brain tickler? | A loud bell | *A fun puzzle that makes you think | A cold drink | A tiny tickle on your foot
exercise: «The clown's silly face was a real rib tickler.» What does rib tickler mean? | A bone that hurts | A sad story | *A very funny joke or thing | A tickle from a feather
exercise: Oliver says, «My tickler file reminds me when my homework is due.» What is a tickler file? | A list of jokes | A tickle monster game | *A reminder system of notes about things to do | A box of feathers for tickling
test: «Dad is the best tickler in our house.» What does tickler mean here? | A reminder note | A joke | A puzzle | *A person who tickles
test: «That riddle was a real brain tickler, so I had to think hard.» What is the best meaning? | *A fun puzzle that makes you think | A reminder note | A feather duster | A sore throat
exam: «The tickler in my throat made me cough.» Which meaning fits? | A fun puzzle | A reminder note | *A small tickle that bothers you | A joke
